# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build artifacts - regenerable with `make build`, never committed.
data/intermediate/
data/output/*
!data/output/.gitkeep
# s0's linkage-engine parquets ARE committed (the data contract; s0 itself
# needs an external corpus not in this repo). s8's acquisition parquets are
# NOT: s8 has no external dependency and regenerates byte-identical output
# from RISK_SEED on every build, so freezing a copy would only risk drift
# between the generator and a stale snapshot.
data/input/acquisitions.parquet
data/input/project_stages.parquet
# s11's feature matrix is an ML-internal artifact placed in data/input/ only
# so pipeline paths stay simple; it is not part of the DB contract (s6/s14
# never read it) and regenerates byte-identical from RISK_SEED every build.
data/input/features.parquet
# Trained models ARE committed: they are small, and a fresh clone must be able
# to serve without retraining (design spec s12).
!data/output/models/

# Cached source snapshots are committed so the demo never touches the network,
# but keep the directory shape even when empty.
!data/raw/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Agent scaffolding
.superpowers/

# Source gazette PDFs: megabytes each, and every one is re-fetchable from
# egazette.gov.in by the document id its parsed JSON records. The parsed
# notifications beside them ARE committed, so `make build` needs no network.
data/raw/egazette/pdf/
# Extracted text for the KEPT corpus - a local convenience that lets
# `--reparse` run without the PDFs on a machine that has harvested. Every
# kept document's parsed JSON is committed beside it already, so this adds
# nothing a clone needs.
#
# data/raw/egazette/rejected/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the text
# a rejection was decided from, which is the one thing a clone cannot
# reconstruct: the PDF is never kept on that path, and without the text an
# improved parser can never revisit the decision.
data/raw/egazette/text/
# The repaired CA bundle is a fetched artifact, rebuilt on demand.
data/raw/.cache/
# The store lock names a process that is running right now.
data/raw/.lock
# Half-written files from an interrupted atomic write; the real file is
# either the old one or the new one, never one of these.
.tmp-*.part
